# Build context sent to the (remote) Docker builder on every deploy.
#
# Without this the context was 61 GB across 141k files — `target/` at 46 GB
# and `.claude/worktrees` at 13 GB — uploaded in full for each build. Slow,
# expensive, and it shipped local working state to a remote builder for no
# reason. The Dockerfile builds from source; nothing below is needed.

# Rust build output, rebuilt inside the image anyway.
target/

# Agent working state: worktrees, session transcripts, local settings.
.claude/
.code-review-graph/

# Local dev runtime state.
.dev/
data/
node_modules/
apps/web/node_modules/
apps/web/dist/

# Secrets and local config — `fly secrets` carries these, never the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# History and CI config are not build inputs.
.git/
.github/

# Docs and examples: the image serves the app, not the documentation.
docs/
examples/
experiments/
editors/
